  "notes": "Cause code D (Defective Procedure) governs category per FORM-366 despite narrative describing a hardware leak as proximate trigger; theme captures that the LLRT procedure isolating SDV drains during a known/undetected leak condition was the underlying defect. Previous occurrence (12/15/18) was not itself an LER (no LER/scram resulted), but is captured as a stub LER node per instructions since it is the referenced 'previous occurrence' in Section E; no LER number was given so key uses available date/unit info in lieu of an actual LER number ('2-2018') since none was stated in the narrative. TS 3.3.1.1 modeled as regulatory reference mitigating/governing the scram function, not as a corrective action. RPS modeled as System without EIIS code since none was given in text."
